# Single-Mouse Dense-Keypoint 5 FPS Experiment

This workflow trains the same flat Social Attention architecture on extracted
single-mouse samples. Original sequence IDs are split before extraction, so all
three mice from a source sequence stay in the same train or validation split.

## Hypothesis

If the flat model can preserve a single mouse's pose when social context is
removed, pose errors should improve relative to the triplet dense-keypoint
baseline. If pose errors remain high, the weakness is likely in intra-mouse
keypoint modeling rather than inter-mouse interaction.

## Inspect configuration

```sh {"id":"01M24SINGLEMOUSE5FPSCONFIG","interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python3.13"}
